BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WFF’s Zine Release Party with Good Neighbor at Unicorn Bar! RSVP
  - FREE to Attend
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T000000
DTSTAMP:20260914T020231Z
UID:6a91be39d9172f9c50cda2b4@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:In anticipation of the 27th annual Woodstock Film Festival the
  WFF team has partnered withGood Neighbor\, the Kingston-based independent
  arts\, culture\, and community publication\, to produce a limited-edition
 \, collectible zine to highlight festival venues\, screenings\, and specia
 l events taking place across the mid-Hudson Valley during festival week in
  October.\n\nJoin us for an evening of drinks and community convergence. M
 eet the Good Neighbor and Woodstock Film Festival teams and help us kick o
 ff the countdown to the 27th Annual Woodstock Film Festival!\n\nA cash bar
  and snacks will be available for purchase at Unicorn Bar during the event
 . Stay after for Queer Line Dancing in the ballroom! Admission is separate
  and on $5 - $25 sliding scale.\n\nSpecial Thanks to our Zine Sponsors:\n
 \nBy RSVPing for this event\, you acknowledge and agree that the name and 
 email address you provide may be shared with WFF and Unicorn Bar for its o
 wn communications and records.\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2
 026-all-events?eventId=6a91be39d9172f9c50cda2b4
LOCATION:Unicorn Bar
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a91be39d917
 2f9c50cda2b4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homunculus 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261012T190000
DTSTAMP:20260914T205141Z
UID:6a95b567c1445f8f5e65a046@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:When Mimi's toxic relationship with Clay comes crashing to an 
 end\, her haplessly devoted assistant Bootbutt is tasked with crafting a s
 culpture of her ex.\n\nThis task ignites a chain of love-crossed folly\, r
 ife with mistaken identity\, sorcery\, and the very act of creation itself
 . A surreal\, darkly comic exploration of love\, ego\, and the absurd perf
 ormances we stage for each other.\n\nRarely leaving Mimiâs living roo
 m and the adjacent closet\, Homunculus relies heavily on the flexibility o
 f light\, the set\, and performance to bring the audience through its narr
 ative.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.
 org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a95b567c1445f8f5e65a046
LOCATION:Unicorn Bar
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a95b567c144
 5f8f5e65a046
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Zoo 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T010000
DTSTAMP:20260914T020231Z
UID:6a85e6f6eb5b7ddb41ae0ca0@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Community Presenter:The Overlook News\n\nThe 27th Annual Woods
 tock Film Festival kicks off with the Hudson Valley premiere ofAmerican Zo
 o. The post-screening Q&A features director Tim Travers Hawkins and specia
 l guests\, moderated by Noah Eckstein\, founding editor-in-chief ofThe Ove
 rlook News.\n\nAbout the Film:Every documentary filmmaker dreams of findin
 g a lost archive and hidden history. WithAmerican Zoo\, director Tim Trave
 rs Hawkins found both. This gripping film unravels the hidden history of a
  beloved local attraction – the Catskill Game Farm – and the complex b
 ond between humans and animals. – Jessica Edwards\n\nTim Travers Hawkins
  is an Emmy-nominated documentary filmmaker known for cinematic and invest
 igative nonfiction exploring systems of power\, justice and institutional 
 accountability. His debut feature\,XY Chelsea\, premiered at the 2019 Trib
 eca Film Festival and earned two Documentary Emmy Award nominations. His o
 ther work includesThe MovementforThe Guardian\,Personafor HBO Max\,Burn It
  Down!for Paramount andCapturing the Killer Nursefor Netflix. Hawkins stud
 ied filmmaking at EICTV in Cuba and trained in Latin America with filmmake
 rs Fernando Birri and Pino Solanas. His latest feature documentary\,Americ
 an Zoo\, had its World Premiere at the 2026 Tribeca Festival.\n\nNoah Ecks
 tein is the founding editor-in-chief ofThe Overlook\, a nonprofit news out
 let providing public-service journalism across seven towns in the Catskill
 s. His work has appeared inThe New York Times\,Vogue\,Semafor\,Variety\,Th
 e GuardianandFast Company\, among other national and international publica
 tions.\n\n﻿Director\n\nTim Travers Hawkins\n\nProducer\n\nJulia Nottingh
 am\n\nExecutive Producer\n\nMary Lisio\, Mandy Chang\, Vicki Cooper\n\nCas
 t\n\nWolf Kahler\, Larry Fessenden\n\nEditor\n\nChris A. Peterson\, Ace Pe
 ter Norrey\n\nCinematographer\n\nPatrick Smith\, Joe Bender\, Mik Bakalarz
 \, Mikul Eriksson\, Kelly Adams\, Isaac Mead-Long\n\nComposer\n\nDan Deaco
 n\n\nPremiere\n\nHudson Valley Premiere\n\nRuntime\n\n86 min\n\nYear\n\n20
 26\n\nCountry\n\nUSA\n\nLanguage\n\nEnglish/German\n\nInstagram\n\nView Pr
 ofile\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.o
 rg/2026-all-events?eventId=6a85e6f6eb5b7ddb41ae0ca0
LOCATION:Community Theater
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6a85e6f6eb5b
 7ddb41ae0ca0
END:VEVENT
