BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MASTERCLASS WITH CATHERINE HARDWICKE: FIX IT IN PREP 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T173000
DTSTAMP:20260914T205141Z
UID:6aa1bb66f557af72f6cf64fc@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Catherine Hardwicke’s master class “Fix it in Prep” take
 s you through her process preparing for her films including Thirteen\, Lor
 ds of Dogtown and Twilight -- as well as TV shows including Netflix’s Gu
 illermo del Toro’s Cabinet of Curiosities – “Dreams in the Witchhous
 e” (working with Oscar winning creature and production designers.) She 
 details her prep journey with clips\, storyboards\, shot lists\, shooting 
 diagrams\, and behind the scenes rehearsals. She explains how she works wi
 th costume designers\, production designers\, and cinematographers to find
  a visual language for each film. She’s presented the workshop at USC\,
  NYU\, Design Center\, Sundance Labs (where she’s been an advisor for 11
  summer labs)\, and multiple film festivals including Tribeca\, TIFF\, VIF
 F\, London Screenwriter’s Festival\, and the Rio de Janeiro Film Festiva
 l.\n\nCatherine Hardwicke directed the acclaimed Thirteen\, cult-classic L
 ords of\n\nDogtown\, and blockbuster Twilight - launching a $3.3 billion f
 ranchise. Her latest\n\nfilm\, Street Smart\, explores young creatives sur
 viving on Venice Beach.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woods
 tockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1bb66f557af72f6cf64fc
LOCATION:Utopia Studios
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1bb66f557
 af72f6cf64fc
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DEMOCRACY IN DOCUMENTARY 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T200000
DTSTAMP:20260914T205141Z
UID:6aa1ba453e8fcdbaebbd2a4f@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:As corporate news consolidation accelerates and independent jo
 urnalism faces growing challenges\, documentaries are filling a critical g
 ap. Even as shifts within the documentary industry reshape how nonfiction 
 stories are funded\, distributed\, and seen\, the form remains a powerful 
 force for public understanding and civic engagement. With the 2026 midterm
  elections approaching\, what role can documentaries play in strengthening
  an informed public—and what responsibility do filmmakers have in protec
 ting democracy?\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilm
 festival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1ba453e8fcdbaebbd2a4f
LOCATION:Utopia Studios
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1ba453e8f
 cdbaebbd2a4f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE PODCAST WITH AMY GOODMAN & AVI ZEV WEIDER: FEATURING MARK DUP
 LASS & KATIE ASELTON 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261016T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T010000
DTSTAMP:20260914T205141Z
UID:6aa1be2c843a0b27c5b431cf@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:Every filmmaker carries with them the ghosts of films that nev
 er came to be — the abandoned scripts\, impossible casting dreams\, proj
 ects that collapsed in financing\, or stories that proved simply too stran
 ge\, ambitious\, or ahead of their time to make.. Through conversation\, a
 rchival development materials\, and speculative reimaginings\, the series 
 revisits the unrealized films that continue to haunt their creators and as
 ks what those unfinished works can still reveal about artistic ambition\, 
 industry gatekeeping\, and the creative process itself. Part confessional
 \, part creative autopsy\, and part speculative resurrection\, FILMS NOT M
 ADE offers a rare glimpse into the hidden archive of cinema: the stories t
 hat almost were — and the unfinished ideas that continue to shape the on
 es that get made. In this special live recording of the podcast\, hosts Am
 y Hobby and Avi Zev Weider invite a filmmaker into a candid excavation of 
 a project they couldn’t quite bring to life.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Availabl
 e\n\n🔗 https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be
 2c843a0b27c5b431cf
LOCATION:Utopia Studios
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be2c843a
 0b27c5b431cf
END:VEVENT
